### Full flow: create order -> check status -> get payment

@orderServiceUrl = http://localhost:8080
@paymentServiceUrl = http://localhost:8081

###
# Step 1 - Create order (copy "id" from response into @orderId below)
POST {{orderServiceUrl}}/orders
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "customer_id": "cust-scenario",
  "item_name": "MacBook Pro",
  "amount": 99999
}

###
# Step 2 - Set the returned order ID
@orderId = 8d047ef5-7bc8-4c4e-9cd2-9261ded51f6a

###
# Step 3 - Verify order is Paid
GET {{orderServiceUrl}}/orders/{{orderId}}

###
# Step 4 - Verify payment is Authorized
GET {{paymentServiceUrl}}/payments/{{orderId}}

###
# Step 5 - Try to cancel a Paid order (expect 409)
PATCH {{orderServiceUrl}}/orders/{{orderId}}/cancel

### ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
### Idempotency scenario
### ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

###
# Request 1 - Create order with idempotency key
POST {{orderServiceUrl}}/orders
Content-Type: application/json
Idempotency-Key: idem-scenario-001

{
  "customer_id": "cust-idem",
  "item_name": "iPad",
  "amount": 80000
}

###
# Request 2 - Exact same request (expect same order returned, no duplicate)
POST {{orderServiceUrl}}/orders
Content-Type: application/json
Idempotency-Key: idem-scenario-001

{
  "customer_id": "cust-idem",
  "item_name": "iPad",
  "amount": 80000
}

### ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
### Failure scenario: Payment Service unavailable -> 503
### (stop payment-service container before running this)
###   docker compose stop payment-service
### ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

###
# Order should fail with 503, order.status = "Failed"
POST {{orderServiceUrl}}/orders
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "customer_id": "cust-fail",
  "item_name": "Widget",
  "amount": 5000
}